<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Viewport</span><span style="text-align:justify;">&#160;</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.663%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>Viewport is the window where user can see the data in three-dimensional space. 3D data are presented in orthogonal projection. There are three ways of displaying objects – as points, wireframe, and as flat or smooth shaded surfaces.</p>
<p><span style="text-align:justify;">Viewport window consists of the following elements:</span></p>
<ul class="whs4">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Title bar</b></span> – if the viewport is a new document then its name is Scan DataN, where N is the number of the subsequent newly opened document. Otherwise it has the name of the file that is open.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:none;"><u style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><b>Scroll bars</b></span></u> – they are two horizontal and one vertical that are used for rotate and pan. There is a button in the lower right corner for switching between <span class="Mode">rotate</span> and <span class="Mode">pan</span> modes. These elements can be hidden. <a href="Scroll_Bars.htm" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:none;"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></a></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Viewable area</b></span> – this is the area where the data are displayed.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Co-ordinate system icon</b></span> – it is located in the upper left corner of the viewable area. It shows current orientation of the viewport.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:none;"><u style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><b>Viewport context menu</b></span></u> – right clicking anywhere on the viewable area and scroll bars will show this menu. <span lang="EN-GB">It contains visualisation commands like zoom, render mode, etc.</span> <a href="viewport_context_menu.htm" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:none;"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></a></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Status bar</b></span> - on the bottom of the viewport. Displays information about the current units in KUBE, additional information about scanning and help.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Viewport</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP175018733" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../working_with_data/visualisation_files/viewport.gif" width="865px" height="617px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p>While holding the left mouse button on the viewable area, user can perform rotate, pan, or zoom of the viewport depending on the current mode.</p>
